<p>When you ask someone about hot, happening real estate markets, there are a few places that come to mind right off the bat: New York City. San Diego. Los Angeles. East coast and west coast. Real estate investors imagine having their hands in such prestigious real estate markets with beach side properties and high-end apartment lofts in the middle of the country&rsquo;s biggest, most bustling cities.</p>
<p>For the investors that get there and love it: great! But there are hidden gems among the many lauded real estate markets: they&rsquo;re not just promising, they&rsquo;re already&nbsp;<em>booming.&nbsp;</em>Opportunities for investors of all types abound, from turnkey investments and single-family homes to commercial real estate and high-demand apartments in the middle of a metropolitan downtown.</p>
<p>So instead of looking east and west, we&rsquo;re setting our sights somewhere in the middle: Houston real estate, Dallas real estate and Memphis real estate. A close look at the market conditions, trends and contributing factors to the health of their local housing markets reveals these three to be not only great candidates for real estate investing, but models of post-recession recovery.</p>
